  "text": "My issues 3 My sessions 1 Dashboard Development Issues Projects Knowledge Project memory Releases Releases Hosted environments Agent management Agents Runtimes Skills Usage Settings NocoBase Studio v1.0.0-beta.75 Agents Demo mode · Switch account 3 SA Agents Add agents from the models runners report. The Lead Agent hands each step of an issue to them by what they are good at. Lead Agent Arranges every issue once it starts: hands each step to an agent, reads the replies and decides what comes next; it moves the issue to Blocked when it needs you and to In review when the work is done. Settings Name Lead Agent Runs with Claude · Opus 5.5 fallback Codex · GPT-6.1 Sol Allocation principles Built-in Comment run limit 20 per issue every 24 hours Agents from runners Add agent Show disabled Agent Good at Where it runs Reasoning effort Status Edit Claude · Opus 5.5 Designs, architecture, hard investigations and reviews of important changes. 2 shared runners Build server build-01, Alex’s MacBook Pro Medium Enabled Edit Claude · Sonnet 5 Frontend pages and components (React, Tailwind, i18n), well-scoped fixes and tests. 2 shared · 1 personal Build server build-01, Alex’s MacBook Pro, Lisa’s workstation Medium Enabled Edit Codex · GPT-6.1 Sol Larger implementations, changes across packages, refactoring and independent review of frontend changes. 2 shared runners Build server build-01, Alex’s MacBook Pro Medium Enabled Edit To add an agent, install a coding tool on a runner and sign in to a model you may use: once the runner reports it, add it from Available models by writing what it is good at. An agent only personal runners have works only on issues their owners start. This is a demo. Changes cannot be saved. Everything else works as usual.",
